                "text": "**Analyzing Pixel Data**\n\nI'm currently focused on analyzing pixel data within a matrix. Specifically, I'm examining scenarios where a single non-8 pixel (color C) exists against a background of 8s. My initial tests involve varying input sizes and the position of this non-8 pixel to determine the appropriate output structure. The aim is to map the process of these pixel positions to a given output.\n\n\n**Calculating Border Distances**\n\nI've been calculating distances to borders to understand the output's dimensions. It seems the output rectangle's size isn't directly the distance, but the number of steps to each boundary. Examining examples, I'm noting that the rectangle formed by the boundaries has heights and widths related to the position of the non-8 pixel and the overall input size. It seems I'm forming a conceptual framework for translating these positional distances into rectangle dimensions.\n\n\n",
